  "description": "DEFECT 1, PRESERVED (practice B5). NEXT SENTENCE at :177 transfers control past the period that ends the current sentence, and that period is the one closing the whole PERFORM UNTIL ... END-PERFORM at :206 - not the END-IF two lines below. So the second record, whose TRAN-PROC-TS begins 2022-09-01 and therefore fails the range test at :173-174, does not get skipped: it ends the entire read loop. The third record is never read, the page and grand totals at :202-203 are never written, and the report is left truncated after the first record's detail line with no total of any kind. The out-of-range record is not displayed either, because DISPLAY TRAN-RECORD at :180 sits inside the in-range arm. Turning this break into a continue would make this case fail, which is exactly the point of having it.",
